From 0714d33d1e6a5e9372410a029c938cfd241fdeec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:40:15 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] A borrowed clip's turns go back to rest once no clip writes
 them

A clip from another character model (Basin Battle's borrowed swings) keys bones the unit's
own clips may leave unkeyed: a wrist, the shield's. An unkeyed property keeps its value, so
the borrowed swing's last turn of such a bone stayed for good, and a night elf woman's or a
tauren's shield was left crooked after the first swing. The evaluator now remembers, per
bone, which properties another model's clip wrote last; once no clip writes one, it goes back
to rest (the bind translation, no turn, unit scale: a vanilla M2's rest pose). What the unit's
own clips write is theirs as before, and a rig that never plays a borrowed clip is untouched.

HasActionCombat() is now 11, so the server can tell a client without this to update.
